Activation: spawn a service once, however many callers ask at the same time.

MUST apply after start-service-activation.patch ("u" sorts after "st").

Every libcosmic app asks org.freedesktop.portal.Desktop for the color scheme
as it starts, so cosmic-app-library and cosmic-launcher address the portal
within the same millisecond. Each implicit activation ran `Exec=` itself: two
xdg-desktop-portal frontends came up, each activated its own
xdg-desktop-portal-cosmic backend (60 MB, a full iced runtime), and the
losers of the name race lingered for the rest of the session (measured on
LeandrOS 2026-10-02: frontend pids 208 and 211, backends :busd.60 and
:busd.65 in one login).

Now `activate_service` returns at once when the name already has an owner,
and a name with a spawn in flight is waited for (same `await_name_owner`
bound) instead of spawned again.

